// Definite assignment is a real flow merge, not "any assignment anywhere": a lone `if` may be skipped, so
// the value is not assigned on every path reaching the read. (Both arms assigning IS accepted — see
// tests/slot_assign_then_read.kama.)
fn int main() {
    slot int32 x;
    if (true) { x = 1; }   // only one path assigns
    return x;              // ERROR: not definitely assigned
}
